# Third-party code, and content that is not distributed

ColourWars is MIT licensed (see LICENSE). This file records what in the working
tree is not ColourWars' to license, and what is deliberately absent.

The main menu's Credits page summarises these acknowledgements and the engine's
notice. Full terms remain here, in LICENSE and in the release's `licenses/`
folder. The accepted Paint.exe replacement bank is included in the game and release.

The engine is not covered here. It is a submodule at `external/labrador` with
its own LICENSE and its own NOTICE, and the third-party code it carries —
Microsoft's `DeviceResources` and `StepTimer`, Christer Ericson's collision
routines — is recorded there.

## Code carried in this repository

### rapidjson (MIT)

`external/rapidjson/` is vendored, with its own `license.txt` and `README.md`
beside it. Copyright (c) 2015 THL A29 Limited, a Tencent company, and Milo Yip.

This is a second copy — the engine vendors one too. That is deliberate rather
than an oversight of the split: the engine's is PRIVATE and no engine header
names the parser, so a client that needs one asks for rapidjson on its own
account. This one is asked for on account of the save file, which the game
*writes* — the engine's assets module only reads, and its `JsonValue`
deliberately keeps rapidjson out of a client's translation units, so the level
files need no copy of their own. `game/save.cpp` is the only file here that
includes it.

### Microsoft content tools (MIT)

Three build tools are retained in this repository:

- `scripts/audio/tools/XWBTool.exe` — the wave-bank compiler.
- `game/art/tools/MakeSpriteFont.exe` — the sprite-font compiler.
- `game/art/tools/texconv.exe` — the texture converter.

Source: https://github.com/microsoft/DirectXTK and
https://github.com/microsoft/DirectXTex

`game/directx.ico`, the executable's icon, is the stock icon from Microsoft's
DirectX Visual Studio project templates
(https://github.com/walbourn/directx-vs-templates), under the same licence.
